Package: baxters-soc-ultralight
Version: 1.0.1-3
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Baxters Lab <165753632+Baxterv5@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-gst-plugins-base-1.0,
 python3-pil, python3-pil.imagetk, python3-tk, python3-numpy, python3-opencv, python3-pyautogui,
 python3-pyperclip, python3-requests, python3-xlib, python3-ewmh,
 tesseract-ocr, xdg-utils
Recommends: python3-evdev
Description: SOC Ultralight — multi-agent screen orchestration
 Drives several chat agents on one desktop: reads their windows, routes
 messages between them, and clicks through their interfaces by template match.
 .
 DISTRO interpreter lane (A1 section 2a): it needs gi, which has no PyPI wheel
 and is ABI-bound to the system interpreter, so it does not use baxters-runtime.
 .
 EVERY dependency is declared here rather than fetched. Until 2026-09-25 the
 launcher built a virtualenv and pip-installed into it on first start, which
 could not work once installed -- /opt/baxters/soc-ultralight is root-owned, so
 a normal user's first launch could not create it -- and which reached the
 network at start-up, forbidden by A1 section 7.1.
 .
 Two modules have no Ubuntu package at all (mss, pytesseract). Both are pure
 Python and are VENDORED in the payload under vendor/, with their licences; see
 THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES. tesseract-ocr is the binary pytesseract drives -- without
 it OCR fails at run time while every import succeeds.
 .
 python3-evdev is Recommends, not Depends: it is imported inside a try/except
 that returns False, so its absence costs one input-capability probe and
 nothing else.
